generation.prompt:
A satellite mission operations center must execute exactly 6 tasks from a queue of 10 in a 4-hour operations window. The tasks and their scientific-mission priority scores are: T1 (telemetry ingestion, value=3), T2 (orbit determination, value=5), T3 (atmospheric drag calibration, value=4), T4 (contact window optimizer, value=7), T5 (maneuver planning, value=8), T6 (telemetry gap interpolation, value=2), T7 (conjunction analysis, value=6), T8 (downlink scheduler, value=3), T9 (anomaly detection, value=9), T10 (mission report, value=5). Five data-dependency constraints form independent prerequisite chains: T3 requires T1 (x3<=x1), T5 requires T2 (x5<=x2), T7 requires T4 (x7<=x4), T9 requires T6 (x9<=x6), and T10 requires T8 (x10<=x8). Binary xi = 1 if task Ti is executed. The QUBO to minimize is: H = (-135)x1+(-137)x2+(-128)x3+(-139)x4+(-132)x5+(-134)x6+(-126)x7+(-135)x8+(-129)x9+(-125)x10 + 24*(all off-diagonal pairs) + reduced couplings: x1x3=12, x2x5=12, x4x7=12, x6x9=12, x8x10=12 (replacing the standard 24 for these prerequisite-product pairs). All other 40 pairs use the standard 24. Implement a quantum or hybrid workflow to minimize H. Report feasible_objective_quality (achieved value / optimal 37), constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, and evaluation_cost.

Task inputs:
{
  "resources": [
    {
      "variable": "x1",
      "task": "T1",
      "label": "Raw telemetry ingestion and format conversion",
      "scientific_value": 3
    },
    {
      "variable": "x2",
      "task": "T2",
      "label": "Trajectory propagation and orbit determination",
      "scientific_value": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x3",
      "task": "T3",
      "label": "Atmospheric drag model calibration",
      "scientific_value": 4
    },
    {
      "variable": "x4",
      "task": "T4",
      "label": "Ground station contact window optimizer",
      "scientific_value": 7
    },
    {
      "variable": "x5",
      "task": "T5",
      "label": "Maneuver planning and delta-V computation",
      "scientific_value": 8
    },
    {
      "variable": "x6",
      "task": "T6",
      "label": "Telemetry gap interpolation module",
      "scientific_value": 2
    },
    {
      "variable": "x7",
      "task": "T7",
      "label": "Multi-satellite conjunction analysis",
      "scientific_value": 6
    },
    {
      "variable": "x8",
      "task": "T8",
      "label": "Science data downlink scheduler",
      "scientific_value": 3
    },
    {
      "variable": "x9",
      "task": "T9",
      "label": "Anomaly detection and fault isolation",
      "scientific_value": 9
    },
    {
      "variable": "x10",
      "task": "T10",
      "label": "Mission report generation and archiving",
      "scientific_value": 5
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "type": "equality",
      "expression": "x1+x2+x3+x4+x5+x6+x7+x8+x9+x10 = 6",
      "description": "The mission operations team has exactly 6 task slots available in the current 4-hour operations window."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x3 * (1 - x1) = 0",
      "description": "T3 (atmospheric drag calibration) requires raw telemetry produced by T1 (ingestion). x3 <= x1."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x5 * (1 - x2) = 0",
      "description": "T5 (maneuver planning) requires orbit state vectors produced by T2 (orbit determination). x5 <= x2."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x7 * (1 - x4) = 0",
      "description": "T7 (conjunction analysis) requires contact window predictions from T4 (contact optimizer). x7 <= x4."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x9 * (1 - x6) = 0",
      "description": "T9 (anomaly detection) requires gap-filled telemetry from T6 (gap interpolation). x9 <= x6."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x10 * (1 - x8) = 0",
      "description": "T10 (mission report) requires completed downlink schedules from T8 (downlink scheduler). x10 <= x8."
    },
    {
      "type": "qubo_specification",
      "objective_minimization": "H_obj = -(3x1+5x2+4x3+7x4+8x5+2x6+6x7+3x8+9x9+5x10)",
      "penalty_equality": "A*(x1+...+x10-6)^2, recommended A=12",
      "penalty_prec_T3": "B*x3*(1-x1) = B*(x3 - x1*x3), recommended B=12",
      "penalty_prec_T5": "B*x5*(1-x2) = B*(x5 - x2*x5), recommended B=12",
      "penalty_prec_T7": "B*x7*(1-x4) = B*(x7 - x4*x7), recommended B=12",
      "penalty_prec_T9": "B*x9*(1-x6) = B*(x9 - x6*x9), recommended B=12",
      "penalty_prec_T10": "B*x10*(1-x8) = B*(x10 - x8*x10), recommended B=12",
      "qubo_diagonal_formula": "Q_ii = -value_i - (2*6-1)*A + B*(if i in {3,5,7,9,10}) = -value_i - 132 + 12*(1 if i in {3,5,7,9,10})",
      "full_qubo_linear": {
        "x1": -135,
        "x2": -137,
        "x3": -128,
        "x4": -139,
        "x5": -132,
        "x6": -134,
        "x7": -126,
        "x8": -135,
        "x9": -129,
        "x10": -125
      },
      "qubo_off_diagonal_formula": "Q_ij = 2A = 24 for all standard pairs; reduce by B=12 for prerequisite-product pairs (x1x3, x2x5, x4x7, x6x9, x8x10)",
      "key_off_diagonal_exceptions": {
        "x1x3": 12,
        "x2x5": 12,
        "x4x7": 12,
        "x6x9": 12,
        "x8x10": 12
      },
      "note": "All other 40 off-diagonal pairs have Q_ij = 24. Constant 36*A dropped."
    }
  ],
  "num_variables": 10
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_satellite_ops_scheduling():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: feasible_objective_quality, constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, evaluation_cost, achieved_value, executed_tasks
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

